<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW1-CI-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW1-CI-001" ;
  triage:title "atm-observability unit tests race on process env: lib.rs test sets ATM_LOG=loud while tracing_bridge ac1/ac2 build a bridge in parallel and fail with invalid ATM_LOG value" ;
  triage:description "PR #1179 CI Test (macos-latest) failed tracing_bridge::tests::ac1_warn_and_error_runtime_events_retain_contract_fields and ac2_filters_unlisted_info_and_retains_all_configured_targets at crates/atm-observability/src/tracing_bridge.rs:438 with invalid ATM_LOG value loud. The value comes from the parallel test at crates/atm-observability/src/lib.rs:240 (EnvGuard::set_many ATM_LOG=loud). Same test binary, shared process env, no serialization. Not reproducible locally in 5 runs; it is a real ordering race, not AW.2 code. Fix on the AW.2 branch (highest open branch where it blocks CI): make the bridge() helper / prepare_retained_log take the level explicitly in tests, or serialize the env-mutating test with the bridge tests via a shared test lock so no test reads ATM_LOG while another sets it. No changes to production code paths beyond test injection." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-flake" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T04:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T03:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW1-CI-001/AW2-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW1-CI-001/AW2-2> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T08:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

# CLOSURE (phase-aw integration review, quality-mgr): quality-mgr independently confirmed at integrate/phase-aw 517db2459 in /tmp/verify-aw-integration: crates/atm-observability/src/lib.rs and tracing_bridge.rs no longer contain any EnvGuard::set_many/process-env mutation of ATM_LOG in tests -- ATM_LOG resolution is injected via an explicit EnvSource trait (FakeEnvSource in tests), eliminating the shared-process-env race entirely (not merely serializing it). `cargo test -p atm-observability` x5 consecutive runs: all green, no flakes -- fixed in a later round before merge, never recorded as closed.

